abstract: >
  The Bibliographic Reference Ontology (BiRO) is an ontology
  structured according to the FRBR model to define
  bibliographic records (as subclasses of frbr:Work) and
  bibliographic references (as subclasses of
  frbr:Expression), and their compilations into
  bibliographic collections such as library catalogues, and
  into bibliographic lists such as reference lists in
  journal articles, respectively.
